  "title": "A Uniform Upper Bound for the Diagonal Maximal-Planar Ramsey Number of K1,3 disjoint union K2",
  "batch_label": "66",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "Let H=K_{1,3} disjoint-union K_2, with copies understood as ordinary (not necessarily induced) subgraphs. Every red-blue edge-colouring of every finite simple maximal planar graph G with |V(G)| at least 21 contains a monochromatic copy of H. Equivalently, P(21) holds and r_MP(H,H) exists with r_MP(H,H) at most 21. No claim is made that 21 is the least threshold.",
